WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:20.064
Aladdin opened the door, and the magician stepped into the house.

2
00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:25.271
"Aladdin, son of my brother!" said Magrib.

3
00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:30.643
He placed a basket of figs into Zeba's arms, bowed low, and said,

4
00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:36.604
"Wife of my brother! A small gift."

5
00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:39.568
Then he looked around the room.

6
00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:44.103
"Tell me," he said, "where did your husband once sit?"

7
00:00:44.104 --> 00:00:48.297
Zeba pointed to a cushion by the wall.

8
00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.141
"Oh, my poor brother!"

9
00:00:51.142 --> 00:00:56.615
Magrib cried out—and collapsed into a heap on the cushion.

10
00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:58.985
"This looks like true sadness,"

11
00:00:58.986 --> 00:01:03.104
whispered Zeba, and she rushed to her guest.

12
00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:06.819
"There's no need to be so distressed," she said.

13
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.232
"Come, let's eat!"

14
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:15.789
Aladdin helped the magician stand up, and his mother carried in the food.

15
00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.749
Then, while they sat and ate, she began to question Magrib.

16
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.273
"Sir, why have I never heard of you before this day?"

17
00:01:25.274 --> 00:01:28.808
"It is no surprise to me," answered Magrib.

18
00:01:28.809 --> 00:01:33.533
"I left this town, my birthplace, forty years ago."

19
00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:37.813
"My husband was still a boy!" said Zeba.

20
00:01:37.814 --> 00:01:39.134
Magrib nodded.

21
00:01:39.135 --> 00:01:42.737
"I wandered through many lands," he continued.

22
00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:47.055
"At last, I found my way to Egypt."

23
00:01:47.056 --> 00:01:51.728
"I've heard it is a wonderful place!" said Aladdin.

24
00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:53.550
"Yes, my boy, it is.

25
00:01:53.551 --> 00:01:58.736
But over time, I became old and homesick for my own country.

26
00:01:58.737 --> 00:02:03.772
I wanted to see my younger brother one more time before my death.

27
00:02:03.773 --> 00:02:06.039
So I journeyed home to find him.

28
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:14.012
But I'm too late!" Magrib began to sob.

29
00:02:14.013 --> 00:02:18.138
"We cannot escape the will of God," said Zeba.

30
00:02:18.139 --> 00:02:20.463
"Here, poor man, eat a bit more!

31
00:02:20.464 --> 00:02:22.778
It will make you feel better."

32
00:02:22.779 --> 00:02:26.652
Magrib took another serving from a big dish.

33
00:02:26.653 --> 00:02:29.180
"I am comforted," he said.

34
00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:36.257
"Even though my brother has gone, he still lives on in this boy, Aladdin."

35
00:02:36.258 --> 00:02:39.824
Magrib put his hand on Aladdin's shoulder.

36
00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:43.923
"Nephew, you are the head of this house," he said.

37
00:02:43.924 --> 00:02:45.924
"What work have you learned to do?

38
00:02:45.925 --> 00:02:49.023
How do you take care of your good mother?"

39
00:02:49.024 --> 00:02:53.659
Feeling guilty, Aladdin looked at his mother.

40
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.745
"He has learned nothing," the widow said angrily.

41
00:02:57.746 --> 00:03:02.641
"Nothing at all. All day, he plays games in the streets.

42
00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:07.630
His father died of sadness because this boy would not work."

43
00:03:07.631 --> 00:03:11.914
Then she burst into tears.

44
00:03:11.915 --> 00:03:19.558
"I am the one who works all day and night to take care of this lazy boy!"

45
00:03:19.559 --> 00:03:26.255
Aladdin hung his head in shame, while the magician smiled and comforted the widow.

46
00:03:26.256 --> 00:03:29.228
"Your troubles are over," he said.

47
00:03:29.229 --> 00:03:33.680
"God has blessed me with wealth so that I may help you."

48
00:03:33.681 --> 00:03:38.958
Aladdin looked up brightly, and his mother wiped away her tears.

49
00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.233
"My nephew, you must learn a business," said Magrib.

50
00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:48.555
"It is a disgrace to play all day while your old mother toils."

51
00:03:48.556 --> 00:03:53.031
"You are right, my uncle," Aladdin said quietly.

52
00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.676
"Now, boy, don't worry,"

53
00:03:54.677 --> 00:03:58.562
said Magrib, patting Aladdin on the shoulder.

54
00:03:58.563 --> 00:04:01.478
"I will buy you a shop and fill it with goods.

55
00:04:01.479 --> 00:04:07.249
Then you can be a merchant—buying, selling, and growing rich!"

56
00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.055
"A merchant?" said Aladdin.

57
00:04:10.056 --> 00:04:16.873
"Growing rich?" added his mother.

58
00:04:16.874 --> 00:04:21.431
She clapped her hands, embraced her son, and whispered into his ear,

59
00:04:21.432 --> 00:04:25.030
"This man must truly be your uncle!"

60
00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:29.416
"I have eaten enough, and it is now late," said Magrib.

61
00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:33.711
"But I will return in the morning, and we will go to the bazaar.

62
00:04:33.712 --> 00:04:40.286
I will buy Aladdin everything he needs to be a young merchant!"
